        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          For software engineers and photographers who want to understand the exact technical mechanics: TakeoutFix operates across three client-side phases.
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <!-- Phase 1 -->
          <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-950 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">PHASE 01</span>
              <span>How TakeoutFix finds your files (Local Directory Indexing)</span>
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Using the W3C File System Access API, the engine traverses directory trees asynchronously via background Web Workers. It indexes media assets into high-performance in-memory hash maps while indexing candidate sidecars to avoid main-thread UI jank.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Phase 2 -->
          <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-950 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">PHASE 02</span>
              <span>Matching media with its metadata (Heuristic Pairing)</span>
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Google Takeout introduces edge cases including truncated 47-character names, copy numbers, and edited suffixes. The heuristic resolves these variants before performing a schema integrity check against the JSON <code class="font-mono text-xs">photoTakenTime.timestamp</code> field.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Phase 3 -->
          <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-950 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">PHASE 03</span>
              <span>How metadata is restored (Binary Header Injection)</span>
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Once matched, the engine writes Unix epoch timestamps and coordinates into native binary headers: <code class="font-mono text-xs">DateTimeOriginal</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs">CreateDate</code>, and GPS IFD blocks for JPEG/HEIC/PNG, and QuickTime user-data atoms (<code class="font-mono text-xs">udta</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs">mvhd</code>) for MP4/MOV videos without re-encoding.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
